<%# locals: (fits_at:, leading: nil, classes: nil) %>
<%# A form's button row: the block's buttons, led by an edit screen's Delete trigger in `leading`. `fits_at` is the row width in rem at which its buttons fit at an equal share, measured in Chromium for the labels the caller draws and rounded up. %>
<%# WHY: the row is its own container because whether its buttons fit is a question about its width, not the viewport's, and the form around it is `contents`, so it cannot be one. CSS cannot measure the labels, so each caller states the width; the classes are spelled out because Tailwind only compiles class names it finds whole in the source. %>
<%# WHY: `flex-col-reverse` puts Save on top of the stack while the DOM keeps the one-line order, so only the stacked row runs focus bottom to top. %>
<% one_line = {
     14 => "@[14rem]:flex-row @[14rem]:*:flex-1",
     18 => "@[18rem]:flex-row @[18rem]:*:flex-1",
     19 => "@[19rem]:flex-row @[19rem]:*:flex-1",
     29 => "@[29rem]:flex-row @[29rem]:*:flex-1",
     35 => "@[35rem]:flex-row @[35rem]:*:flex-1"
   }.fetch(fits_at) %>
<%= tag.div class: [ "@container", classes ] do %>
  <div class="flex flex-col-reverse gap-2 <%= one_line %>">
    <%= leading %>
    <%= yield %>
  </div>
<% end %>
